# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KLEOS Training Data .gitignore
#
# This repository is PRIVATE, and private git is not a secure data vault. These
# rules are a safety net, not a substitute for judgement. Before committing:
#
#     python scripts/check_no_private_data.py .
#
# See SECURITY.md, PRIVACY.md and DATA_GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# NOTE ON COMMENTS: git does not support trailing comments in .gitignore.
# "!data/fixtures/  # note" is a literal pattern that matches nothing, which
# silently un-ignores nothing at all. Every comment here is on its own line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The three zones are ALL deny-by-default --------------------------------
#
# staging/ holds unverified captures and partially sanitized candidates.
# vault/   holds the entity vault and surrogate maps — the re-identification keys.
# releases/ holds finished datasets, which are the product and are shipped by
#          path, not by git (spec section 4.1).
#
# `<dir>/*` rather than `<dir>/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so "staging/" followed by "!staging/.gitkeep" would
# silently drop the .gitkeep and the directory would vanish from the repo.
#
# Only the top-level .gitkeep is tracked. The subdirectories are runtime state
# created by `python scripts/init_workspace.py`, not repository content.
staging/*
!staging/.gitkeep
vault/*
!vault/.gitkeep
releases/*
!releases/.gitkeep
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep

# --- data/ is DENY-BY-DEFAULT -----------------------------------------------
#
# An allowlist on purpose. A blocklist ("ignore *.jsonl") only blocks the
# filenames someone thought of in advance — drop a real export in as
# data/my_export.json and it sails straight into a commit.
data/*
!data/README.md
# Fictional surrogate name pools. Synthetic, committed on purpose.
!data/surrogates/
# Tiny valid/invalid corpora for contract and differential tests.
!data/fixtures/
# The id collision ledger. Contains hashes and assigned ids, no content.
!data/id_ledger.json

# --- Split filenames at the repository root ---------------------------------
#
# releases/ is already ignored wholesale, so this only catches a dataset
# copied or downloaded to the wrong place. Deliberately root-anchored: the
# public repo's global `**/train.jsonl` rule would erase this repository's
# entire product.
/train.jsonl
/validation.jsonl
/test.jsonl

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.hf_token
.huggingface/

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# --- Tooling ----------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# --- Local agent notes ------------------------------------------------------
claude.md
CLAUDE.md
